    "created_at": "2023-05-07T10:49:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-07T10:49:18Z",
    "body": "That makes sense, I guess for clarity `AllowSharedBufferSource` would be better, to indicate it's allowed, but not enforced.\r\n Defined as:\r\n```webidl\r\ntypedef (SharedArrayBuffer or [AllowShared] BufferSource) AllowSharedBufferSource;\r\n```\r\nI think that works because `[AllowShared] ArrayBuffer` would end up ignored. Though we could flatten it a bit more if that would be preferred:\r\n```webidl\r\ntypedef (ArrayBuffer or SharedArrayBuffer or [AllowShared] ArrayBufferView) AllowSharedBufferSource;\r\n```\r\ncc @Constellation",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
